          "name": "chart_from_csv",
          "canonical_hash": "sha256:29ff31795606c35a483340b8c9d6d744af5fd53f5bf7d325eb25e1639e4f8ac8",
          "description": "Parse raw CSV text and generate a chart directly from it, without requiring the caller to pre-process the data. The tool auto-detects numeric columns for the y-axis and uses the first non-numeric column as x-axis labels. Use this when the user provides CSV content directly; for data already in a Python list or dict use create_chart instead.",
